                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "371c2d19-9ff5-31a5-a979-2e086b4539c5",
                        "entry_id": "cad1a5d0-e6e6-378f-9160-12081ef71e7f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "спец. содержащий колчедан, характерный для колчедана либо имеющий к этому минералу иное непосредственное отношение; то же, что колчедановый"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe5d90e4-037c-4dbc-bae7-f8f0f41b947a",
                                "sense_id": "371c2d19-9ff5-31a5-a979-2e086b4539c5",
                                "text": "Эта тенденция в полной мере проявлена на колчеданных месторождениях."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99abe3fb-d41e-4c1a-af4c-9462f23ff1b1",
                                "sense_id": "371c2d19-9ff5-31a5-a979-2e086b4539c5",
                                "text": "Новый тип колчеданного оруденения на Северном Кавказе."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f1eef8aa-a70c-4d57-a217-ae494175efaf",
                        "source_entry_id": "cad1a5d0-e6e6-378f-9160-12081ef71e7f",
                        "source_sense_id": "371c2d19-9ff5-31a5-a979-2e086b4539c5",
                        "target_lang_word": "pyrite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pyrite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d9c8a08-99e7-3aaf-9019-3f1a8aed4a17",
                                        "entry_id": "9321d760-7860-3880-aff6-2f1fee41aada",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The common mineral iron disulfide (FeS₂), of a pale brass-yellow color and brilliant metallic luster, crystallizing in the isometric system."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b42506f4-06c0-4ad4-b9ba-cef8a56da70c",
                                                "sense_id": "5d9c8a08-99e7-3aaf-9019-3f1a8aed4a17",
                                                "text": "The pyrite output in 1961 was 1.2 million tons, derived mainly from the Hsiang Shan mine in Anhwei and the Ying-te mine in Kwangtung."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebbae260-25a1-4c23-8114-d8d232237ffc",
                                                "sense_id": "5d9c8a08-99e7-3aaf-9019-3f1a8aed4a17",
                                                "text": "China's 13 large foreign fertilizer plants ordered a few years ago are all scheduled to be in operation in a year or two.[…]China's biggest pyrite mine (openpit), being built in Yunfu, Kwangtung Province, was near completion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09f97eb2-5835-32d4-b2bd-29eb70f94846",
                                        "entry_id": "9321d760-7860-3880-aff6-2f1fee41aada",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any metallic-looking sulphide, such as the above, which is the most common."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c683f4f-af33-3e0d-9b20-107c12330cc3",
                                        "entry_id": "9321d760-7860-3880-aff6-2f1fee41aada",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "(usually as a plural: pyrites) Any metal dichalcogenide that is isostructural to the common mineral."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "776f77f0-4f78-4972-95bb-7e0d434704e4",
                                                "sense_id": "7c683f4f-af33-3e0d-9b20-107c12330cc3",
                                                "text": "Copper diselenide can occur both as a marcasite and a pyrite."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d3dc1405-20ca-40d2-a81b-bcfd38b87b3f",
                        "source_entry_id": "cad1a5d0-e6e6-378f-9160-12081ef71e7f",
                        "source_sense_id": "371c2d19-9ff5-31a5-a979-2e086b4539c5",
                        "target_lang_word": "sulfur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sulfur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "631bbfc3-db82-3a70-b3b1-5fb9a5c53c4e",
                                        "entry_id": "7d2427ab-2ca8-30b1-b52a-5df036b4f0bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A chemical element (symbol S) with an atomic number of 16, having a bright yellow color and characteristic smell, used commercially in a variety of products such as insecticides, black powder, and matchsticks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c0e168b-8982-4087-aca4-58b174702f09",
                                                "sense_id": "631bbfc3-db82-3a70-b3b1-5fb9a5c53c4e",
                                                "text": "A Dungeon horrible, on all ſides round / As one great Furnace flam’d, yet from thoſe flames / No light, but rather darkneſs viſible / […] but torture without end / Still urges, and a fiery Deluge, fed / With ever-burning Sulphur unconſum’d:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82f5deb9-c612-4e6d-8cfe-ee125e6b1e42",
                                                "sense_id": "631bbfc3-db82-3a70-b3b1-5fb9a5c53c4e",
                                                "text": "Sure only that man is mortal; that with the life of one mortal snaps irrevocably the wonderfulest talisman, and all Dubarrydom rushes off, with tumult, into infinite Space; and ye, as subterranean Apparitions are wont, vanish utterly,—leaving only a smell of sulphur!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1edc2ac2-7a8b-4782-b5bb-b3aa6849b822",
                                                "sense_id": "631bbfc3-db82-3a70-b3b1-5fb9a5c53c4e",
                                                "text": "Scarcely had these manifestations ceased at Ustica, than Vesuvius began to show signs of increased activity; the supplies in the wells on the mountain sides began to fail, and there was observed a strong taste of sulphur in the drinking water; whilst—most dreaded phenomenon of all—the ever-active crater of Stromboli, that lies midway between Naples and Messina, suddenly lapsed into quiescence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f3a5173-a992-41e6-b9f2-72798ad30a11",
                                                "sense_id": "631bbfc3-db82-3a70-b3b1-5fb9a5c53c4e",
                                                "text": "It went like this: first, we were cavemen, then there was ancient Greece, then Rome burned (cue sulfur-odor FX), then there was the Great Depression, and, finally, we reached the modern age."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c78b8798-dfb0-4fe4-bf91-1b4df86c3733",
                                                "sense_id": "631bbfc3-db82-3a70-b3b1-5fb9a5c53c4e",
                                                "text": "Local workers hike up the side of the mountain and down into the crater at the top to harvest its sulfur—a byproduct of the gas that escapes from the volcano’s vents and collects near the shores of an acidic lake at the crater’s center. The chemical is used in industry worldwide, from making matchsticks to vulcanizing rubber, but Ijen’s sulfur goes mostly to local factories, which use it to bleach sugar."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43c3ec74-71cc-387d-b615-fc961f725807",
                                        "entry_id": "7d2427ab-2ca8-30b1-b52a-5df036b4f0bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A yellowish green colour, like that of sulfur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf963d43-d49e-3ce8-9208-6460f8c15ffb",
                                        "entry_id": "7d2427ab-2ca8-30b1-b52a-5df036b4f0bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various pierid butterflies of the subfamily Coliadinae, especially the sulfur-coloured species."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
